From: KB2UKA <kb2uka@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: reset: match optional SMC state cells

The current macsmc-reboot driver accepts absent state cells. It explicitly
allows shutdown_flag to be missing for newer hardware and guards each cell
access. Keep the four-cell layout when supplied, but allow the pair of
properties to be omitted. J713 Abbey offsets have not been established;
this does not copy another PMIC family's offsets or assert stay-off behavior.

This binding-only change does not alter the kernel binary or its ABI.

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/reset/apple,smc-reboot.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/reset/apple,smc-reboot.yaml
@@ -35,4 +35,6 @@
+dependencies:
+  nvmem-cells: [ nvmem-cell-names ]
+  nvmem-cell-names: [ nvmem-cells ]
+
 required:
   - compatible
-  - nvmem-cells
-  - nvmem-cell-names
